        "Abstract": "We present a new multilingual task-oriented dialogue dataset, MTOP, with 117 intents and 78 slots across 6 languages. We study compositional generalization in a few-shot setting, where we train on a subset of languages and evaluate on the remaining languages. We find that compositional generalization is challenging for current models, and that a simple approach of translating the English training data to the target language can significantly improve performance. We also show that using a masked language model can further improve performance."
